    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34714" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-cognosco</span></b> , nōvi,
			nĭtum, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to become perfectly acquainted
			with</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 1, 2, 50</span></i>
			 (Speng. pergnovi).— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percognĭtus</span></b> , a, um,
				P. a., <i>well known</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex naturae non ignota, etsi nondum percognita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 45, 45, § 116</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Germania,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					14, 28, § 98</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">37, 3, 11,
				§ 45</span></i>.</div>
